<Base title="About The Belt Equation: why I built it, how the odds are worked out, and what has moved them" description="Why I built a public model of my odds of living and working in space, how the number is worked out from the tree, and every change to it so far.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Why I built this, and how it works</h1>
    <p class="lede">I'm John, 40 years old, and I write about AI, sentience and the spread of conscious life beyond Earth at <a href="https://sentient-horizons.com" rel="noopener">Sentient Horizons</a>. I want to leave the planet before I die, and I'd rather know my real odds than keep the wish vague. So I built the probability tree behind this site. It puts a number on the wish and it shows me which links are likely to move in the next few years, so I know where to watch, and which ones would move the odds most.</p>
    <p>The name comes from the Belters of the TV series <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Expanse_%28TV_series%29" rel="noopener"><em>The Expanse</em></a>, the people who live and work in the asteroid belt, far from Earth. Underestimated, and at home where nobody thought people could be. I want to see a solar system like that unfold. This site works out, in public, how likely that is. The longer story is in <a href="https://sentient-horizons.com/essays/the-belt-equation/" rel="noopener">the essay that introduced the project</a>.</p>
